1. twitter-text 3.1.0
   https://github.com/twitter/twitter-text
   Copyright 2011 Twitter, Inc.
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).

   What is used:
   - The regular expressions that find links, including the list of domain
     endings, and the weights in config/v3.json. They are reproduced in
     src/core.js, which tools/build-core.mjs assembles from the package's
     compiled output.
   - The steps of extractUrlsWithIndices, idna.toAscii and parseTweet, which
     src/core.js follows.
   - The conformance cases in test/fixtures/twitter-text-conformance.json,
     taken from conformance/validate.yml, extract.yml and tlds.yml at commit
     30e2430d90cff3b46393ea54caf511441983c260.

   What was changed:
   - The expressions are assembled from named parts in one file rather than
     loaded one per file, and characters outside ASCII are written as escapes.
     The assembled expressions have the same source text as the originals.
   - The link expression is tried one position at a time, behind a check that
     skips positions where it cannot match. The links found are the same.
   - The surrounding code is rewritten without the library's helper modules,
     and Punycode encoding is implemented here from RFC 3492 instead of using
     the punycode package.
   - The conformance cases are converted from YAML to JSON; only the sections
     about weighted length and link extraction are included.

